          <declname>_Neighbours</declname>
        </param>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Gets a list of all the nearest neighbour vertices of a vertex. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername direction="in">_Vertex</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Target vertex to retrieve the neighbours of.</para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername direction="out">_Neighbours</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Pointer to a user-allocated array of <ref refid="ndxlcore_8h_1ad03a49b11a22416ba63273c4d7deb38b" kindref="member">NDXLVertex</ref> pointers. The array must contain at least ndxlGetVertexDegree(_Vertex) elements. The function populates the array in-place.</para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="return"><para>If either _Vertex or _Neighbours are NULL, returns <ref refid="group__ndxl__err_1gae9261a8e1c9a6cebdc947ee5798cca1e" kindref="member">NDXL_ERR</ref>, otherwise populates _Neighbours with the nearest neighbour vertex pointers of _Vertex, and returns NDXL_OK.</para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="note"><para>The caller retains ownership of the array, but not of the <ref refid="ndxlcore_8h_1ad03a49b11a22416ba63273c4d7deb38b" kindref="member">NDXLVertex</ref> objects referenced by its elements. These pointers refer to the original objects in the owning network of _Vertex, so modifications through them affect those objects directly. The returned list can be used to modify or destroy its referenced objects without invalidating the array itself.</para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="warning"><para>The function does not verify the capacity of the supplied array. Providing an inadequately sized array can result in out-of-bounds writes and undefined behaviour.</para>
</simplesect>
