          <declname>_Edge</declname>
        </param>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Gets the time-delayed state vector of a neighbouring vertex. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername direction="in">_Vertex</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Target vertex to retrieve the neighbour state of.</para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername direction="in">_Edge</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The edge connecting _Vertex to its neighbour, the latter of which will be queried for its time-delayed state.</para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="return"><para>If either _Vertex or _Edge are NULL, or _Edge is not connected to _Vertex, returns NULL, otherwise returns the delayed state vector of the neighbouring vertex to _Vertex along _Edge.</para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="note"><para>If the delay of _Edge is zero, this is equivalent to calling ndxlGetVertexState(ndxlGetVertexNeighbour(_Vertex, _Edge)).</para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="note"><para>If the delay of _Edge is nonzero, this function uses historical states stored by _Edge to lookup the state of the neighbouring vertex at time t - ndxlGetEdgeDelay(_Edge). If the requested time does not fall exactly on a stored state, the function performs a cubic Hermite interpolation between the two surrounding states and returns the interpolated state.</para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="note"><para>In both cases, the returned pointer is shared, meaning it remains valid over the lifetime of the vertex, but the stored values will change on subsequent calls to this function.</para>
</simplesect>
